	(text "Current sense output:\nScaling Factor: 0.25V/A (8A = 2V)\nCutoff Frequency: 800Hz\nGain Error: about +-2% \n    (+-1% due to shunt resistor tolerance, \n    +-1% due to INA180 input filter)\nOffset Error: about +-25mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 166.624 128.016 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "335840ad-e580-435b-a085-3f7da961cf25")
	)
	(text "Approx power budget:\nAssume the following usages:\n- 3.3V regulator: 8A @ 3.3V at 90% efficiency: 29.33W\n- 5V regulator: 8A @ 5V at 90% efficiency: 44.44W\n- Each card: 100mA on V_{SUPPLY}\n\nThis gives that Vsupply must be able to supply about 74W + 800mA, or\nabout 4A @V_{SUPPLY}=24V or about 9A @ V_{SUPPLY}=9V. I'm going to\nfudge that a little and say that our max current is 8A (so that we\ncan use the same current sense circuit as the other rails and so we stay\nunder the limit for this barrel jack)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.294 54.356 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d3888582-bcff-4e88-8031-4c9b325e7dff")
	)
	(text_box "Power may be connected via barrel jack (more standard, works with COTS power supplies) or via Mini-Fit connector (more mechanically robust, same connector series as used on the cards)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 97.79 0)
		(size 35.56 16.51)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
